# Real game files the tests read, staged next to the test executable by
# tools/code_emit/build_emit.py.  8.3 names, one per line.
#
# ICON.CEL is the unit sprite sheet: 1920 sprites of 24x24 in 160 groups of
# twelve, read by tests/rsrc.c's cover for fdps_cache_cel_sprite_group.  That
# reader takes a fixed 0x2970-byte bite out of the sheet's offset table, so it
# needs a real sheet -- a fabricated one large enough to survive that read
# would be a copy of this file with different numbers in it.
ICON.CEL
#
# FIELD2.VFS is the smallest .VFS the game ships at 112,350 bytes, read by
# tests/vfs.c's cover for fdps_vfs_read_entry_count.  That reader takes the
# entry count straight out of a container's header, so the assertion is only
# worth anything against a container whose header the game actually wrote.
FIELD2.VFS
#
# MISC.VFS is the container fdps_load_data_tables reads: the nine .dat members
# it names are in this file and in no other one the game ships, so tests/main.c
# cannot pin filename-to-global pairing against anything smaller.  A load that
# misses would not fail the assertion either -- the loader's wrapper ends the
# process -- which is the other reason the real container is the only usable
# input here.
MISC.VFS
#
# FIELD.VFS is the container fdps_deploy_wave loads its MAP%02d.COD placement
# table out of, and it cannot be stood in for.  A missing container sends that
# function into fdps_wait_any_key, which spins until a keyboard interrupt that
# never comes, and a container missing the member the map number names sends it
# into exit(1) -- neither failure is one an assertion can catch.  The
# coordinates the cases in tests/deploy.c expect are the placement records
# inside this file's own MAP00.COD and MAP01.COD.
FIELD.VFS
#
# FIELD1.VFS holds the tile maps, the tile sheets and the per-cell event-code
# layers, so it is the third of the three containers
# fdps_field_load_chapter_resources opens.  That function takes no argument and
# formats every member name itself, so there is nothing to point at a smaller
# file, and a member it cannot find sends fdps_vfs_load_entry into
# fdps_wait_any_key and then exit(1) -- neither of which an assertion can
# catch.  The cases in tests/rsrc.c skip themselves unless all three
# containers are present.  It is the largest file staged here at 8.9 MB, and it
# is copied once: the staging step leaves a file whose size already matches
# alone.
FIELD1.VFS
#
# FDE.SAV is the save file the game ships, 0x59cb bytes of ciphertext, read by
# tests/save.c's cover for fdps_xor_crypt_buffer.  It is the only witness that
# covers the whole keystream: decrypted in place it has to yield a plaintext
# whose checksum equals the dword the file itself stores at +0x59c7, and all
# 22,983 keystream bytes have to be right for that to hold.  A fabricated save
# would be ciphertext this test produced with the code under test, which proves
# nothing.
FDE.SAV
#
# FACE.CEL is the portrait sheet: 160 records of 125x100, read by tests/msgwin.c's
# cover for fdps_load_and_draw_portrait.  That routine holds the sheet's name as
# a literal and takes no file argument, so nothing can point it at a smaller
# fixture, and a sheet it cannot open ends the process at exit(1) rather than
# failing an assertion.  The record offsets, lengths and decoded pixels the
# cases expect are this file's own.
FACE.CEL
#
# The four blend tables and the three combat containers are what
# fdps_combat_play_attack_exchange reads, and none of them can be stood in for.
# The two .tmp pairs are opened by bare name with the result untested, so a
# missing one faults inside fread rather than failing an assertion; the
# containers are opened through fdps_vfs_load_entry, which ends the process on a
# member it cannot find.  What tests/combat.c asserts is that the names the
# function composes out of a record byte -- Stand%03d.saf, Act%03d.saf and
# Back%02d.saf -- reach the members the shipped containers hold, and the lead-in
# counts that separate a standing attack from a travelling one are ACT000.SAF's
# and ACT005.SAF's own.
FMER1.TMP
FMER2.TMP
MER1.TMP
MER2.TMP
FIGHT.VFS
FIGACT.VFS
BACKGRND.VFS
